    "longTermBackground": {
      "summary": "User is an SRE/Ops practitioner working with gateway, Nginx, and dispatch/power-grid (调度数据网, MSTP, WAMS, 钟山电厂) infrastructure, with established workflow patterns around log-based alert analysis (ERROR/WARN spike detection, error pattern clustering, risk attribution, 未复归 vs 已复归 alarm classification). The user communicates in Simplified Chinese, prefers concise direct markdown reports without clarification questions, and is actively building a multi-agent + skill ecosystem with named personas (天璇数字员工, yunxin/云心) and named skills (alarm_analysis), each with defined SOUL.md/spec files, distinct operational scopes, and explicit coordination boundaries. The user has a consistent behavior pattern of opening sessions with casual '你好' greetings on weekday mornings and weekends, expecting 天璇数字员工 to autonomously identify next steps and proactively suggest concrete tasks with structured status boards (3-tier ✅/⏳/🔴 + priority menu), progressively migrating recurring prompts into named skills while extending outputs downstream into leadership-facing artifacts (PPT) using minimal-swiss executive style. User has formalized HITL confirmation expectations and committed to Feishu Interactive Card + 自建应用 Open API as the notification transport — with ask_clarification being the in-session HITL tool, complemented by Feishu as the cross-channel HITL tool. User has demonstrated a methodical, evidence-driven debugging pattern: when investigating failures (e.g., the RAGFlow 'NoneType' bug), they systematically rule out environmental/query-level causes via controlled probes before localizing root cause to the server side. However, on 2026-10-04 a new data point (successful RAGFlow retrieval of README_zh.md content) challenges the prior 'deterministic server-side NoneType bug' diagnosis — suggesting the bug may be narrower than previously concluded (perhaps only affecting chat_answer, not retrieval), or that re-validation is needed.",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-04T15:55:56.251851Z"
    }
