      "id": "fact_d191b7da",
      "content": "RAGFlow's chat endpoint failure mode (2026-10-01) is a deterministic server-side code bug — the server performs a subscript access against `None` during the chat_answer serialization (likely `response[\"data\"][\"answer\"]` where one of the keys returns `None`). The failure occurs regardless of: (a) whether the KB is empty or has documents, (b) whether the query is meaningful or just 'hello', (d) whether the session was freshly created. This is NOT a client-side issue, NOT a query relevance issue, and NOT a knowledge-base contents issue.",
      "category": "knowledge",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T16:32:35.757966Z",
      "source": "65732edf-1a14-4369-8396-a66c3e533ad3"
    },
    {
      "id": "fact_a1a6a17a",
      "content": "Two mitigation paths proposed for the RAGFlow chat_endpoint 'NoneType' bug (2026-10-01): (A) server-side fix — enter /opt/ragflow and inspect logs via `docker compose logs -f ragflow` (or corresponding process stdout) to locate the stack trace for the 'NoneType' subscript exception, then diagnose which of LLM config missing / Embedding model unloaded / retrieval component not started is responsible, and apply the corresponding fix or restart. (B) bypass the chat endpoint — RAGFlow MCP currently exposes only 3 tools (list_datasets / create_chat / chat) with NO retrieval-class interface (retrieve/search); short-term workaround is to HTTP-call RAGFlow's retrieval API `/api/v1/retrieval` directly, bypassing the broken chat path.",
      "category": "knowledge",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "createdAt": "2026-10-01T16:32:35.757966Z",
      "source": "65732edf-1a14-4369-8396-a66c3e533ad3"
    },
